{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nPass 1 (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/pass1.py`, `passes.pass1_chunk`, prompts `reviewers/plan_review_finder.md` + one `plan_review_<ID>.md` per criterion, routing in `criteria_routing.json`, frontier class = Opus on Bedrock) is the expensive pass. A criterion edit cannot be judged from stored data alone, so Tier 2 re-runs finders on a small fixed sample. Per-criterion edits are far cheaper in single-criterion mode; prior work (`docs/experiments/plan-review-model-tradeoff.md`) showed Opus is flat to 12 criteria/turn while Sonnet degrades.\n\n**Execution tier is per-criterion, not uniformly single-turn.** `registry.exec_tier(crit)` (registry.py:604) returns `\"AGENT\"` for any id in `AGENT_TIER` (`{\"G1G2\",\"E4\",\"A1\",\"G6\",\"T5c\",\"T10\",\"T11\",\"G3\",\"G4\"}`, registry.py:97) or `\"CONTAINER\"` for `G3`/`G4` (container fan-out via `pass1_container`); everything else is single-turn (`pass1_chunk`, `agentic=False`). `T5c` is AGENT-tier — it runs agentically (multi-turn, tool-using), NOT the \"$0.17 single-turn chunk\" the naive cost model assumes. Single-criterion mode uses `production_batch_runner`'s REAL routing: `req.with_inputs[\"probe_criteria\"] = {<id>}` on a `BatchRunRequest`, which `_resolve_criteria` splits into `single`/`agent`/`skipped` via `exec_tier` automatically — the SAME dispatch production uses, not a bespoke \"single-turn chunk of one.\" Cost varies by the resolved tier: single-turn criteria cost ≈ $0.17-0.25/sample (the AC's ceiling); AGENT/CONTAINER-tier criteria cost their real production rate (no fixed ceiling assumed) and are reported separately in the ledger, not folded into the single-turn AC.\n\n**Tier-1 chaining, corrected.** `tier1.replay_review` requires a STORED `verification` on each finding (`f.get(\"verification\")`) to build `stored_answers` — a freshly-generated Tier-2 candidate finding has none, so Tier-1's `per_question_agreement`/`distribution_shift` (which compare stored-vs-candidate ANSWERS) cannot run on it directly. Instead, Tier 2's \"downstream\" reuses Tier-1/Tier-0's COMPUTATION functions, not their AGREEMENT functions: candidate findings are verified fresh via the SAME `verify_findings` seam Tier-1 uses (producing real verifications), then `review_kernel.decide.pass3_decide`/`pass3_over_findings` computes a CANDIDATE VERDICT from them. That candidate verdict is compared against the STORED verdict already recorded in the original review's sidecar (`data[\"findings\"]`'s own persisted decisions) — a verdict-level comparison (flip matrix, same shape as Tier-0's), not a per-question agreement table.\n\n## Approach\n\nBuild `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier2.py`:\n\n- **Fixed sample**: ~20 review ids drawn once by the Tier-1 stratified sampler (additional strata: ≥5 containers, ≥8 with ≥10 findings, ≥3 from the LMN store), committed as `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/tier2-sample.json`. Plan text from reconstructed material; code-grounded AGENT criteria run against the pinned `verified_at_sha` snapshot via `source=attested`.\n- **Full mode**: run the candidate registry/prompts through `ProductionBatchRunner`/`run_pass1`, frontier class pinned to Bedrock Opus; compare candidate Pass-1 finding sets to stored findings by `norm_id` (Jaccard, gained/lost per criterion); verify candidate findings via `verify_findings` (Tier-1's seam) and compute their verdict via `pass3_decide`/`pass3_over_findings`; compare to the stored verdict (flip matrix, per Context above).\n- **Single-criterion mode**: `--criteria T5c` sets `probe_criteria={\"T5c\"}` on a `BatchRunRequest` and runs it through `production_batch_runner`/`_resolve_criteria` (real single/agent/container dispatch) over the sample; compares only that criterion's findings. Cost per criterion depends on its resolved `exec_tier`.\n- Baseline for a criterion whose stored findings predate the current `regver`: a one-time baseline run recorded in the ledger; otherwise stored findings are the baseline.\n- Budget pre-flight from stored per-criterion usage (`coverage.usage.per_criterion`) × current price.\n\n`src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/__main__.py`: add a `tier2` subparser (`--candidate <registry-dir>`, `--criteria <id>`, plus shared `--store`/`--cache-dir`/`--out-dir`) and a `_run_tier2` dispatch branch, mirroring `tier0`/`tier1`.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/tier2.py` (new)\n- `src/rebar/llm/evals/plan_replay/__main__.py` (edited — `tier2` subparser + dispatch)\n- `docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/replay/tier2-sample.json`, `tier2-*.md` (new/generated)\n- `tests/unit/evals/test_plan_replay_tier2.py` (new)\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit: with a `FakeRunner` returning canned `P1Output`, gained/lost findings per criterion match expectations; single-criterion mode for a single-turn id issues exactly one chunk per sampled review; single-criterion mode for an AGENT-tier id (e.g. `T5c`) dispatches agentically via `production_batch_runner` and is NOT forced single-turn; a run is refused when the frontier model is not the Bedrock Opus id; the sample file is validated against the corpus manifest; a candidate finding set is verified via `verify_findings` and its verdict computed via `pass3_decide`, compared correctly against a fixture's stored verdict. Live (commissioning, ≤$60): one full-mode baseline over the fixed sample. `__main__.py`'s `tier2` subcommand dispatches correctly.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A committed fixed sample of review ids exists with the strata above; checked by the sample file and manifest cross-check.\n- [ ] `tier2 --candidate <registry-dir>` produces finding-set Jaccard and gained/lost-per-criterion tables plus a candidate-vs-stored verdict flip matrix; checked by one generated report.\n- [ ] `tier2 --criteria <single-turn-id>` costs ≤ N × $0.25 in the ledger; checked by the ledger. An AGENT/CONTAINER-tier `--criteria` run is priced at its real production rate and reported separately, with no fixed per-sample ceiling assumed.\n- [ ] Commissioning spend for this ticket ≤ $60 and every call uses the Bedrock frontier model id; checked by the ledger.\n- [ ] Unit tests pass in `make test`."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788122244294144011,"uuid":"a553953b-cc83-46d9-9c3b-22bbd99e8392"}